  "invariants": [
    "UAR owns admission, dispatch lineage, result recording and uncertain-outcome reconciliation for UAR work.",
    "Flint Gate or the P1 trusted host owns policy decisions, issuer-scoped approval identities and grant revisions, but does not perform effects.",
    "Governed execution fails closed and visibly when policy, required facts, identity, current grant, approval, lease or budget is missing or invalid.",
    "Authority is re-evaluated after every durable wait and immediately before admission.",
    "Admission is recorded before connector dispatch.",
    "Unknown dispatched outcomes remain uncertain and are reconciled without automatic replay.",
    "constrained-local is explicitly selected and never an automatic fallback."
